# Ancient Vendetta: "Unlike similar cards, Ancient Vendetta allows you to choose the name of a basic land. Note that you may only
# search for up to four cards with the chosen name, even if you find more of them" and "You don't have to exile each card you find
# with that name. If you want to leave one in their graveyard, for example, you may." Bot1 names Island. Bot2 has an Island in its
# graveyard (discarded to hand size on turn 2), seven in its hand and the rest of a library of Islands. Bot1 takes none from the
# graveyard, four from the hand (the limit), so no library search is asked (nothing more can be found).
# The Island stays in the graveyard, the hand keeps three, and the library, searched for nothing, is whole.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Ancient Vendetta
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x8
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Cleanup]
Bot2.Discard(Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancient Vendetta.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Name(Island)
Bot1.Choose()
Bot1.Choose(Island; Island; Island; Island)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot2.Graveyard = Island
Bot2.Hand = Island; Island; Island
Bot2.Library.Count = 12
